resilience4j:
  circuitbreaker:
    instances:
      receiveTreasuryCB:
        registerHealthIndicator: true
        eventConsumerBufferSize: 10

        # 🔒 CLOSED State Configuration
        # If failureRateThreshold is reached within this many calls, it will OPEN
        slidingWindowType: COUNT_BASED
        slidingWindowSize: 10              # Check the last 10 calls
        failureRateThreshold: 50           # If 50% of them fail → OPEN the circuit
        minimumNumberOfCalls: 5            # Only start evaluating after 5 calls

        # 🔓 OPEN State Configuration
        waitDurationInOpenState: 5s        # Stay OPEN for 5 seconds before moving to HALF-OPEN

        # 🔁 HALF-OPEN State Configuration
        permittedNumberOfCallsInHalfOpenState: 3    # Allow 3 trial requests
        automaticTransitionFromOpenToHalfOpenEnabled: true  # Move to HALF-OPEN automatically

  retry:
    instances:
      receiveTreasuryCB:
        maxRetryAttempts: 3
        waitDuration: 2s
🔍 What Happens at Each Stage?
State	Controlled By	Behavior
CLOSED	slidingWindowSize, failureRateThreshold	Normal traffic allowed. If failures hit 50%, circuit goes OPEN.
OPEN	waitDurationInOpenState	No calls are allowed. All go to fallback. Waits 5s before testing again.
HALF-OPEN	permittedNumberOfCallsInHalfOpenState	Tests 3 calls. If they succeed → go back to CLOSED. Fail → back to OPEN.
